#* {{quote-book|en|year=1948|chapter=7|title=w:A Russian Journal|author=w:John Steinbeck|isbn=9780141905839|oclc=715891|publisher=The Viking Press|location=New York|passage=During our stay in '''Georgia''' Mr. Chmarsky's gremlin hardly operated at all, and that made us feel better toward him, and made him feel better toward us.}}

